1
00:00:14,980 --> 00:00:19,380
The following tale begins on
June 5th in the year 1972.

2
00:00:20,540 --> 00:00:24,937
It was a dark and humid night in
America's deep south when the first

3
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:29,138
cry of a newborn child rang through
the halls of a maternity hospital.

4
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:31,430
However,

5
00:00:31,513 --> 00:00:34,277
before that baby had the
chance to see the light of day,

6
00:00:34,360 --> 00:00:36,007
his life expired while still

7
00:00:36,820 --> 00:00:38,217
curled in the arms of his mother.

8
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:39,476
To the young mother,

9
00:00:39,640 --> 00:00:42,057
who had never once felt that
she had been living a life

10
00:00:42,140 --> 00:00:45,077
that consisted of any
happiness or sense of purpose,

11
00:00:45,160 --> 00:00:46,480
her newborn son

12
00:00:47,120 --> 00:00:50,597
was going to be a symbol of the hope
that she would have a better future.

13
00:00:50,680 --> 00:00:52,720
With her first child lost to her,

14
00:00:52,940 --> 00:00:55,857
that potential happiness she
longed for was lost as well,

15
00:00:55,940 --> 00:00:57,880
and she was unable to accept

16
00:00:58,940 --> 00:00:59,770
his death.

17
00:00:59,853 --> 00:01:03,537
Before the doctors and nurses could
learn of the baby's unfortunate passing,

18
00:01:03,620 --> 00:01:08,177
the young mother slipped out of her bed
as if she were a phantom in the night.

19
00:01:08,260 --> 00:01:10,677
She made her way into
another room where she

20
00:01:10,760 --> 00:01:13,348
replaced her deceased
child with one who was

21
00:01:13,960 --> 00:01:16,517
born the same day and made him her own.

22
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:19,440
This other baby which
she took was one of a set

23
00:01:20,060 --> 00:01:21,057
of fraternal twins.

24
00:01:21,140 --> 00:01:24,846
To this day, the incident was
never questioned or investigated,

25
00:01:25,100 --> 00:01:27,820
and not Even a single
soul suspected a thing.

26
00:01:31,860 --> 00:01:33,760
Mama, whose grave is this?

27
00:01:34,140 --> 00:01:36,260
They were born the same day as me.

28
00:01:37,020 --> 00:01:38,180
Died then, too.

29
00:01:39,440 --> 00:01:40,520
Enrico. Huh?

30
00:01:41,360 --> 00:01:44,940
The truth of the matter is,
you had a younger brother.

31
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:48,040
The two of you were fraternal twins. Huh?

32
00:01:48,540 --> 00:01:52,011
But he passed away at the
hospital right after he was born.

33
00:01:53,580 --> 00:01:54,560
Pray for him.

34
00:01:56,800 --> 00:02:00,500
Afterwards, we decided to
give him the name Dominic.

35
00:02:06,180 --> 00:02:08,180
Lord, answer my plea.

36
00:02:08,840 --> 00:02:12,840
My brother and I were born on the
same day, but I lived and he died.

37
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:17,420
For what reason did fate choose to
take my brother's life and not mine?

38
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:22,180
And why do humans experience
happiness and misfortune?

39
00:02:22,980 --> 00:02:24,700
What is true happiness?

40
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:28,660
At this time, Enrico was age 15.

41
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:32,840
His great-grandmother on his father's
side was an Italian immigrant.

42
00:02:33,260 --> 00:02:37,057
He is descended from a prestigious
and influential family in Venice,

43
00:02:37,140 --> 00:02:38,797
in which one of his family members became

44
00:02:38,880 --> 00:02:42,180
a famous clergyman during
the 18th century. So,

45
