rat me out to the police.

77
00:04:18,400 --> 00:04:20,224
Is that what you want me to do?

78
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:25,497
Though a thief wouldn't lie about a
sun allergy, it doesn't seem plausible.

79
00:04:25,580 --> 00:04:28,462
Not even the devil would
tell such a blatant lie.

80
00:04:29,100 --> 00:04:30,120
Hold on a moment.

81
00:04:30,560 --> 00:04:34,320
Did you just twist your ankle
because of me? Are you all right?

82
00:04:34,620 --> 00:04:35,740
No, it isn't that.

83
00:04:36,120 --> 00:04:37,377
Please don't worry about it.

84
00:04:37,460 --> 00:04:39,417
I've been like this since my birth.

85
00:04:39,500 --> 00:04:42,617
They say I was born with
twisted toes on my left foot.

86
00:04:42,700 --> 00:04:45,406
However, it doesn't
hinder my ability to walk.

87
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:51,226
Do you believe in gravity
between individuals?

88
00:04:51,720 --> 00:04:54,217
You ended up tripping
over me, of all people.

89
00:04:54,300 --> 00:04:56,476
But did you know it was for a reason?

90
00:04:58,180 --> 00:04:59,356
What are you saying?

91
00:05:04,660 --> 00:05:05,720
Take this arrow.

92
00:05:06,160 --> 00:05:08,042
Consider it a thank you present.

93
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:12,478
If you do not wish to accept it,
that is still perfectly fine with me.

94
00:05:12,860 --> 00:05:16,331
But are not all meetings of
fate their own form of gravity?

95
00:05:16,520 --> 00:05:21,340
We only did just meet, so I don't know
what your first impression of me is.

96
00:05:21,520 --> 00:05:25,108
But I am a traveler fueled by
the hope of fateful encounters.

97
00:05:25,300 --> 00:05:28,120
If ever you feel like
seeing me again someday,

98
00:05:28,600 --> 00:05:31,640
