final breath, I traded him for another.

119
00:06:49,120 --> 00:06:54,100
While no one was looking, I took a
stranger's baby and left mine in his place.

120
00:06:54,860 --> 00:06:56,480
That baby was a twin.

121
00:06:58,580 --> 00:07:02,360
When I think about the baby's
parents, I am overcome with guilt.

122
00:07:03,960 --> 00:07:08,100
Though he wasn't mine, I raised the
child to the best of my ability.

123
00:07:09,060 --> 00:07:10,600
I was so happy,

124
00:07:10,880 --> 00:07:15,645
and the little boy I watched go through
life grew up to be such a fine young man.

125
00:07:16,160 --> 00:07:16,990
However,

126
00:07:17,073 --> 00:07:22,240
if I die without ever confessing, what
would happen if I told him the truth,

127
00:07:22,460 --> 00:07:24,342
that he has a brother somewhere?

128
00:07:24,640 --> 00:07:26,837
Though if he finally learns what happened,

129
00:07:26,920 --> 00:07:29,626
that would mean I've
lost my son before I die.

130
00:07:32,100 --> 00:07:35,960
Are you familiar at all with who
the family of the other son is?

131
00:07:36,760 --> 00:07:40,760
The other twins' family live in a
big mansion in the next town over.

132
00:07:41,820 --> 00:07:43,820
Poochie is the family's last name.

133
00:07:46,540 --> 00:07:48,177
I, like, really don't get it.

134
00:07:48,260 --> 00:07:51,257
What exactly do you see in that
juice delivery boy, anyway?

135
00:07:51,340 --> 00:07:52,170
I know.

136
00:07:52,360 --> 00:07:53,654
But that butt, though.

137
00:07:53,780 --> 00:07:55,080
Just stop it already.

138
00:07:55,340 --> 00:07:57,657
I bet the loser comes from a poor family.

139
00:07:57,740 --> 00:07:59,477
He probably doesn't
even go to high school.

140
00:07:59,560 --> 00:08:01,266
That's why he delivers juice.

141
00:08:02,420 --> 00:08:03,280
Hey, Perla!

142
00:08:03,500 --> 00:08:04,657
Doesn't that bag belong to you?

143
00:08:04,740 --> 00:08:05,570
No!

144
00:08:05,653 --> 00:08:06,483
That guy just took it!

145
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:08,240
He's a purse snatcher!

146
00:08:08,540 --> 00:08:10,060
Someone catch that guy!

147
00:08:20,720 --> 00:08:21,900
God damn it.

148
00:08:22,220 --> 00:08:24,749
I ended up breaking
out the store's window.

149
00:08:25,240 --> 00:08:27,475
Totally gonna get fired from this job.

150
00:08:27,580 --> 00:08:30,815
Plus, I'm not even allowed
to work under school policy.

151
00:08:31,380 --> 00:08:34,380
Weather Forecast's real
name is Wes Aquamarine.

152
00:08:34,920 --> 00:08:36,740
He was 16 at the time,

153
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:41,706
