a strong belief in the idea of justice.

154
00:08:42,660 --> 00:08:44,520
So, uh, thanks a bunch.

155
00:08:45,020 --> 00:08:46,860
You saved my purse back there.

156
00:08:47,980 --> 00:08:51,627
Don't worry, I'll tell them he's
the one who broke the window.

157
00:08:51,840 --> 00:08:52,670
Real?

158
00:08:53,360 --> 00:08:54,217
Yes, of course.

159
00:08:54,300 --> 00:08:55,460
Now you should go.

160
00:09:00,120 --> 00:09:02,260
Um, my name's Wes.

161
00:09:02,580 --> 00:09:04,097
Some people call me Weather.

162
00:09:04,180 --> 00:09:05,540
You wanna hang?

163
00:09:10,400 --> 00:09:14,477
Two months had passed since the dying
mother's life-changing confession,

164
00:09:14,560 --> 00:09:16,854
and Enrico was in utter mental turmoil.

165
00:09:17,580 --> 00:09:19,874
Although he hadn't become a priest yet,

166
00:09:19,980 --> 00:09:22,317
Enrico was still bound
by the seal of confession

167
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:24,960
and could not disclose anything to anyone.

168
00:09:25,700 --> 00:09:28,340
He had to keep it a secret at all costs.

169
00:09:28,740 --> 00:09:33,211
Otherwise, in the eyes of the church,
he would be a failure as a man of God.

170
00:09:34,180 --> 00:09:39,121
That mother will die soon, and she's going
to take her secret with her to the grave.

171
00:09:39,380 --> 00:09:42,439
Even if I could convince
her to confess to everyone,

172
00:09:43,280 --> 00:09:46,300
would we, or at the very
least, would my brother,

173
00:09:47,140 --> 00:09:51,434
